# CI Gate Before Milestone Completion

Do not declare a milestone, feature, or substantial change finished until the full local CI suite has passed.

## Required Gate

Run `task ci` before considering milestone work done. This mirrors GitHub Actions:

- Backend: Ruff, Black, MyPy, Pytest (`ci:backend`)
- Desktop: typecheck, unit, smoke, Vite build (`ci:desktop`)
- Frontend: lint, typecheck, build (`ci:frontend`)

Linux-only Tauri packaging is excluded from local parity; everything else must pass.

## When This Applies

- Completing a numbered milestone from the roadmap/status docs
- Finishing a multi-file feature or bugfix that would land on main
- After fixing CI failures that previously blocked merge

## Expectations

- Fix failures in the same change; do not hand off known red CI
- Prefer `task ci` over ad-hoc single-package checks when closing work
- If a step cannot run locally (missing Docker/Postgres, etc.), say so explicitly and still run every check that can run
- Do not claim “CI is green” from partial runs (for example only Ruff, or only unit tests)
